;;
;; 2. cljs exception aliases: (def Exception js/Error) and kin in
;;    #?(:cljs ...) blocks, used as throw/catch types in the cljs
;;    pass. Carve's bundled kondo does not credit the cljs-only
;;    defs' uses; the fleet kondo with both passes does.
eve.db.ds.db/Exception
eve.db.ds.db/UnsupportedOperationException
eve.db.ds.test.components/Throwable
eve.db.ds.test.explode/Throwable
eve.db.ds.test.parser-find/Throwable
eve.db.ds.test.parser-return-map/Throwable
;;
;; 3. Public library surface with no in-repo caller at this pin:
;;    bset's lookup and est-count are upstream persistent-sorted-set
;;    API (est-count is the documented size path for Iter-backed
;;    sets); query's normalize-pattern-clause is a public fn of the
;;    query engine namespace. db's unfiltered-db is the public
;;    accessor that unwraps a FilteredDB to its underlying DB.
eve.db.ds.bset/lookup
eve.db.ds.bset/est-count
eve.db.ds.query/normalize-pattern-clause
eve.db.ds.db/unfiltered-db
;;
;; 4. util/if+ is called inside util.cljc's own macro machinery
;;    (cond+ expands through it); hook-blind carve cannot see the
;;    use.
eve.db.ds.util/if+
;;
;; 5. Entry points reached by name from outside static analysis:
;;    the browser runner's run-suite/init are called from the test
;;    page; contract.one-cljs/main is the node entry; the query-v3
;;    test's run-regressions! is a script entry; eve.db.ds.test's
;;    test-node is invoked by name to shell to the node test runner.
eve.db.ds.browser-runner-main/run-suite
eve.db.ds.browser-runner-main/init
contract.one-cljs/main
eve-db-ds-query-v3-test/run-regressions!
eve.db.ds.test/test-node
;;
;; 6. Referenced by qualified symbol inside query DATA (the stored
;;    query-fn fixtures): the query engine resolves the symbol at
;;    runtime; no static call exists.
eve.db.ds.query-fns-test/sample-query-fn
eve.db.ds.test.query-fns/sample-query-fn
